      "factual_description": "Park Avenue Armory presents Music for 18 Musicians: Staged Variations in the Wade Thompson Drill Hall from Wednesday, October 14 through Sunday, October 18, 2026. Wednesday through Saturday performances begin at 7:00 PM and Sunday begins at 3:00 PM; the production runs approximately three hours and thirty minutes. The Armory frames the production around both the 50th anniversary of Music for 18 Musicians' premiere and Steve Reich's 90th birthday. Alan Pierson stages and music-directs a cycling durational version that brings together the original Steve Reich Ensemble, Alarm Will Sound and next-generation musicians from Manhattan School of Music, with the musicians encircling the audience and connective interludes by special guest artists. John Heginbotham is credited for movement and associate direction, Urs Schönebaum for lighting design and Mark Grey for sound design. Tickets start at $55 including fees. The current primary page does not name the special guest artists or individual Manhattan School musicians, so none are inferred.",
